1 SYSTEM_VOLUME

   govax keeps its own files on an ODS-2 volume of their own, the system
   volume: by default the container ~/.govax/govax-system.dsk, labeled
   GOVAXSYS, mounted on DUA0: every time govax starts (see STARTUP).  The
   first start makes it from the files built into govax.

2 Contents

     [SYSTEM.SYSEXE]   SYS$SYSTEM     DEFAULT.ROM, PAGEFILE.SYS
     [SYSTEM.SYSMGR]   SYS$MANAGER    STARTUP.COM, SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM,
                                      CONSOLE.DCL, DEBUG.DCL
     [SYSTEM.SYSHLP]   SYS$HELP       HELPLIB.HLB, DBG$HELP.HLB
     [.SOURCES]                       the help libraries' .HLP files
     [.SOURCES.DEBUG]                 the debugger's DEBUG.HLP
     [SYSTEM.SYSLIB]   SYS$LIBRARY,   STARLET.MLB, FORSYSDEF.TLB,
                       SYS$SHARE      FTNRTL.EXE
     [SYSTEM.SOURCES]  SYS$SOURCES    KERNEL.ASM, SSDEF.ASM, FTNRTL's
                                      sources, STARLET.MAR and
                                      STARLETDEF.MAR, BUILDFTN.COM,
                                      BUILDSTARLET.COM, BUILDHELP.COM
     [SYSTEM]          SYS$SYSROOT:   GOVAX$FILES.DAT, the list of
                       [000000]       files govax supplied;
                                      GOVAX$UPDATE.LOG, the log of
                                      what each start updated

   govax defines SYS$SYSDEVICE and SYS$SYSROOT when it mounts the
   volume, and SYS$COMMON and SYS$SPECIFIC, the same root as SYS$SYSROOT;
   STARTUP.COM defines the rest, so you can see and change them.
   SYS$SYSROOT is a rooted name, _DUA0:[SYSTEM.], and concealed, so that
   SYS$SYSTEM is SYS$SYSROOT:[SYSEXE], the directory [SYSTEM.SYSEXE],
   and shown under that name.
   MACRO, FORTRAN, LINK, RUN, and HELP find their libraries, FTNRTL.EXE,
   and the help through SYS$LIBRARY, SYS$SHARE, and SYS$HELP ahead of the
   copies built into govax, so an edited kernel, a rebuilt FTNRTL, a
   rebuilt macro library, or changed help is the one used.

2 Rebuilding

   The procedures in SYS$SOURCES rebuild FTNRTL.EXE, STARLET.MLB, and the
   help libraries from the sources, as new versions:

     $ @SYS$SOURCES:BUILDFTN
     $ @SYS$SOURCES:BUILDSTARLET
     $ @SYS$SOURCES:BUILDHELP

   Delete the versions you made to go back to govax's.

2 Updates

   SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM is yours: govax makes it once and never
   changes it.  Every other file is govax's: when a newer govax has a new
   copy of a file you haven't changed, it writes its copy as a new
   version (the old one stays); a file you have changed is kept, and
   %MOUNT-I-SYSKEPT says so once for each new copy.  The help libraries
   are treated a module at a time: modules you added or changed stay,
   and govax's new modules are added.

   Each file a start writes on an existing volume, and each help library
   module it inserts, replaces, or removes (as LIBNAME(MODULE)), is a
   line in SYS$SYSROOT:[000000]GOVAX$UPDATE.LOG with the time.  The log is made
   when first needed and added to at its end after that.

2 Sharing

   Only one govax session at a time can write the volume; a second
   mounts it read-only (%MOUNT-I-SYSREADONLY), with no page file there.
   DISMOUNT refuses it.  If it can't be used, %MOUNT-W-NOSYSVOL says why
   and govax starts from its built-in files, as it does with the option
   --system-file none.  --system-initialize makes the volume again from
   govax's own files, keeping the old container as FILE.old.  See
   CONFIGURATION KEYS for the settings.
